==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{lbor|en|la|eczema}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἔκζεμᾰ||cutaneous eruption}}, from {{suffix|grc|ἐκζέω|-μᾰ|t1=to boil out, break out|pos2=nominal suffix|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɛk.sɪm.ə/|/ˈɛks.mə/|/ˈɛɡ.zɪm.ə/|/ˈɛɡz.mə/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ɪɡˈzi.mə/|/ˈɛɡ.zəm.ə/|/ˈɛk.səm.ə/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛksɪmə|ɛɡzɪmə|iːmə|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|eczemata|+}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} A [[non-contagious]] [[acute]] or [[chronic]] [[inflammation]] of the [[skin]], characterized by [[redness]], [[itching]], and the outbreak of [[ooze|oozing]] [[vesicular]] [[lesion]]s which become [[encrusted]] and [[scaly]].
#: {{hyper|en|dermatitis}}

